---
import { loadCourse } from "../../lib/course";

const { modules } = await loadCourse();
const first = modules[0];
const capstone = modules.find((m) => m.id === "m7");
---

<section class="mg-how not-content">
  <h2>How a module goes</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><code>uv run miubais start {first.exercise}</code> copies the starter into your workspace.</li>
    <li>
      Read the lesson, write the code, run <code>miubais check</code>. Deterministic tests decide; the stage table on the
      site updates.
    </li>
    <li>
      Stuck? <code>miubais hint</code> explains what the failing test checks. The tutor sees your diff and the test output,
      never the reference solution, and a filter drops anything that leaks it.
    </li>
    <li>
      One stage per module is a judgment call: read the traces, write the taxonomy or the plan. Tests check structure and
      agreement with a key, not prose.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="cta">
    <a class="b" href="/start/">Start here</a>
    {capstone && <a href={capstone.href}>Read the capstone module first</a>}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .mg-how {
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    color: var(--mg-ink);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.625rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  ol {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.375rem;
  }
  li {
    margin: 0.375rem 0;
  }
  code {
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--mg-code-bg);
    font: 0.8125rem var(--__sl-font-mono);
  }
  .cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.875rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 2.125rem;
  }
  a {
    color: var(--mg-link);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  a.b {
    padding: 0.6875rem 1.125rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--mg-ink);
    color: var(--mg-bg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  a.b:hover {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
</style>
